      "answer": "$a=\\frac{12}{5}$.",
      "official_mark_scheme_text": "$g(x)=\\frac12(x^3+4)$. B1 SOI. Either substitute $x=0$: $g(0)=\\frac12(0^3+4)=2$. M1. Then $gg(0)=6$. A1. Evaluate $f(6)=36+24a+a$. M1. Or form a composite using their $g(x)$: $fg(x)=\\left(\\frac{x^3+4}{2}\\right)^2+4a\\left(\\frac{x^3+4}{2}\\right)+a$, or $gg(x)=\\frac{(x^3+4)^3}{16}+2$. M1. Obtain a complete algebraic expression for $fgg(x)$. A1. Replace $x=0$ in their $fgg(x)$. M1. Then $36+24a+a=96$. A1 OE. $a=12/5$. A1 OE. Total: 6.",
